#ifndef WXL_SEAM
#error "define WXL_SEAM(domain, name, symbol, ret, conv, params) before including scrn.def"
#endif

// The EVENT_ID_PAINT handler of Layer.cpp: one call is one frame. When the device has a context
// and the window can be seen, it walks the layers in z-order -- the world and the interface are
// two of them -- has each paint, and presents; otherwise it presents what is there and sleeps.
//
// Before raises FrameBegin, but only on the branch that draws, decided with the same two tests
// the function makes, GxHasContext and GxIsWindowVisible -- the first of which it inlines, at
// 0x004A8723. A minimised client paints nothing, and a frame announced then would be a mod
// drawing with no device. After raises nothing; the frame closes at the present, in
// Gx.ScenePresent, before the image is shown. A frame announces no stage: the paint is
// registered after the script context exists, so ConsoleDevice.Initialize announces graphics.
//
// It is a static of Layer.cpp, but its address is taken -- it is registered as an event handler
// -- so it keeps the convention it is declared with. It never reads its two parameters; they are
// on the stack all the same, pushed and cleaned by its callers (0x004A8BA4 pushes both and
// cleans eight bytes), which is why the row declares them.
WXL_SEAM(Scrn, OnPaint, "OnPaint", int32_t, cdecl, (const void* data, void* param))
WXL_SEAM_RAISES(Scrn, OnPaint, FrameBegin)
